    <section class="content-section">
      <h2>Data Retention During Deletion</h2>
      <p>Some data may be retained for limited periods even after account deletion for the following purposes:</p>

      <table class="data-table">
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th>Data Type</th>
            <th>Retention Period</th>
            <th>Reason</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td><strong>Server Logs</strong></td>
            <td>Up to 90 days</td>
            <td>Security monitoring and abuse prevention</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><strong>Backup Archives</strong></td>
            <td>Up to 30 days</td>
            <td>Disaster recovery (automatically purged)</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><strong>Legal Hold Data</strong></td>
            <td>As required by law</td>
            <td>Legal compliance and regulatory requirements</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>

      <p>Note: Any retained data is anonymized or encrypted and cannot be used to identify you or access your
        content.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="content-section">
      <h2>Deletion Timeline</h2>
      <p>Your account deletion follows this timeline:</p>

      <div class="timeline">
        <div class="timeline-item">
          <h4>Day 0: Deletion Requested</h4>
          <p>You confirm account deletion. Your account is immediately signed out and marked for deletion.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="timeline-item">
          <h4>Days 1-29: Grace Period</h4>
          <p>Your data remains intact but inaccessible. You can cancel deletion by signing back in during this
            period.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="timeline-item danger">
          <h4>Day 30: Permanent Deletion</h4>
          <p>All your data is permanently and irreversibly deleted from our servers. No recovery is possible
            after this point.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="timeline-item danger">
          <h4>Day 30-60: Backup Purge</h4>
          <p>Data is removed from backup systems as they cycle through normal retention periods.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="content-section">
      <h2>How to Cancel Deletion (Recovery)</h2>
      <p>Changed your mind? You can recover your account during the 30-day grace period:</p>

      <div class="success-box">
        <p><strong>✓ Recovery is Simple:</strong> Simply sign back into Better Keep Notes with your Google account
          within 30 days of requesting deletion. Your deletion request will be automatically cancelled and all
          your data will be restored.</p>
      </div>

      <h3>Recovery Steps</h3>
      <ol>
        <li>Open Better Keep Notes on any device</li>
        <li>Tap "Sign In" and use your Google account</li>
        <li>Your scheduled deletion will be automatically cancelled</li>
        <li>All your notes and data will be available again</li>
      </ol>

      <div class="warning-box">
        <p><strong> Time Limit:</strong> Recovery is only possible during the 30-day grace period. After
          day 30, your data is permanently deleted and cannot be recovered by any means.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="content-section">
      <h2>Local Data</h2>
      <p>In addition to server data, Better Keep Notes stores data locally on your device. When you delete your
        account:</p>

      <ul>
        <li><strong>Automatic Cleanup:</strong> Local data is cleared when you are signed out after requesting
          deletion.</li>
        <li><strong>Manual Cleanup:</strong> You can also uninstall the app to remove all local data.</li>
        <li><strong>Other Devices:</strong> Local data on other devices will be cleared when you next open
          the app on those devices.</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>To Manually Clear Local Data</h3>
      <p>If you want to ensure all local data is removed:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Android:</strong> Go to Settings → Apps → Better Keep Notes → Storage → Clear Data</li>
        <li><strong>iOS:</strong> Uninstall and reinstall the app, or delete the app entirely</li>
        <li><strong>Web:</strong> Clear your browser's site data for Better Keep Notes</li>
        <li><strong>Desktop:</strong> Uninstall the application and delete the app data folder</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

