      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="content-section">
      <h2>Before You Delete</h2>
      <p>We recommend taking these steps before deleting your account:</p>

      <ol>
        <li><strong>Export Your Data:</strong> Use the app's export feature to download a backup of your notes
          before deletion.</li>
        <li><strong>Check All Devices:</strong> Make sure you have access to any notes stored only locally on
          other devices.</li>
        <li><strong>Save Important Information:</strong> Copy any critical information to another location.</li>
        <li><strong>Review Shared Content:</strong> If you've shared any notes, inform collaborators before
          deletion.</li>
      </ol>
    </section>

    <section class="content-section">
      <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>

      <h3>Why do I need to verify my email to delete my account?</h3>
      <p>Email verification is an additional security measure to confirm you truly own the account being deleted.
        This protects against unauthorized deletion if someone gains access to your device. We send a 6-digit
        code to your registered email that expires in 10 minutes.</p>

      <h3>I didn't receive the verification code. What should I do?</h3>
      <p>Check your spam or junk folder first. The email is sent from <strong>noreply@betterkeep.app</strong>.
        If you still don't see it after a few minutes, try requesting a new code. Make sure the email address
        on your account is correct and accessible.</p>

      <h3>Can I delete specific notes instead of my entire account?</h3>
      <p>Yes! You can delete individual notes by moving them to trash and then emptying the trash. You don't
        need to delete your entire account to remove specific content.</p>

      <h3>Will my notes be visible to anyone during the grace period?</h3>
      <p>No. Once you request deletion, your account is signed out and your data becomes inaccessible to
        everyone, including you (unless you cancel the deletion by signing back in).</p>

      <h3>Can Better Keep Notes staff access my data during deletion?</h3>
      <p>No. Your notes are end-to-end encrypted. Even our staff cannot read your note contents. The deletion
        process is automated and does not involve human review of your data.</p>

      <h3>What happens if I create a new account with the same email after deletion?</h3>
      <p>After the 30-day period, your old data is permanently deleted. If you create a new account with the
        same email address, it will be a completely fresh account with no access to previous data.</p>

      <h3>How do I know my data has been deleted?</h3>
      <p>After the 30-day grace period, you will not be able to sign into your old account. If you try to
        sign in, you'll be prompted to create a new account, confirming the old account no longer exists.</p>

      <h3>Is there any way to expedite the deletion process?</h3>
      <p>The 30-day grace period is designed to protect you from accidental deletion. If you have urgent
        security concerns, please contact us at <a href="mailto:contact@betterkeep.app">contact@betterkeep.app</a>
        and we'll assist you.</p>
    </section>

